WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.498
Welcome to ADVISIO.

2
00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.004
This walkthrough follows the Faculty
Adviser workspace:

3
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:08.638
accepting research groups, monitoring
their progress, reviewing

4
00:00:08.696 --> 00:00:12.144
manuscripts, providing guidance, and
preserving the records that

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.700
support academic work.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.634
Sign in with your authorized adviser
account.

7
00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.616
Check the Faculty Adviser label and
Adviser Portal badge to confirm

8
00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:21.510
your workspace.

9
00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:25.341
This recording uses fictional
demonstration accounts and research

10
00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:27.721
records in an isolated local
environment.

11
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:31.572
The Overview dashboard brings together
important information about

12
00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:33.221
your advising responsibilities.

13
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.482
From here, you can check research
groups, pending requests, review

14
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.920
activities, and upcoming
consultations.

15
00:00:40.512 --> 00:00:44.482
The sidebar provides access to My
Advisees, manuscript reviews,

16
00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:48.488
official documents, consultations, and
communication tools.

17
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.374
When a research group requests your
assistance as an adviser, the

18
00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:54.174
request appears in your workspace.

19
00:00:54.603 --> 00:00:58.318
Before responding, review the
available group information, research

20
00:00:58.376 --> 00:01:01.372
details, and the message submitted by
the researchers.

21
00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:05.319
If a supporting request form is
attached, you can also examine it

22
00:01:05.377 --> 00:01:06.979
before making your decision.

23
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.164
If you agree to advise the group,
select Accept and complete the

24
00:01:11.199 --> 00:01:11.977
confirmation.

25
00:01:12.569 --> 00:01:16.122
Once accepted, the adviser assignment
is recorded, and the group

26
00:01:16.168 --> 00:01:18.293
becomes available in My Advisees.

27
00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:22.530
If you cannot accommodate a request,
you may decline it and provide

28
00:01:22.553 --> 00:01:23.807
an appropriate response.

29
00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:27.522
The system records the decision so the
researchers can follow the

30
00:01:27.569 --> 00:01:28.939
status of their request.

31
00:01:29.531 --> 00:01:32.851
The acceptance and decline in this
recording use separate fictional

32
00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:33.560
requests.

33
00:01:34.152 --> 00:01:37.832
Confirm each decision only after
reading the request and entering an

34
00:01:37.855 --> 00:01:39.271
appropriate response.

35
00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:42.746
Overview shows your current Advisee
Groups count against the

36
00:01:42.781 --> 00:01:43.954
configured maximum.

37
00:01:44.546 --> 00:01:47.216
Compare these figures when considering
another request.

38
00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:50.571
They describe the workload recorded in
ADVISIO;

39
00:01:51.071 --> 00:01:54.368
they do not replace a discussion about
your actual availability or

40
00:01:54.449 --> 00:01:55.633
research expertise.

41
00:01:56.225 --> 00:01:59.128
This walkthrough keeps the configured
limit unchanged and

42
00:01:59.186 --> 00:02:02.854
demonstrates only the capacity
information displayed to the adviser.

43
00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:06.800
My Advisees provides access to the
research groups assigned to you.

44
00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:10.411
Each group has its own workspace,
where you can review its research

45
00:02:10.445 --> 00:02:14.660
information, documents, milestone
progress, consultations, and

46
00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:15.844
related activities.

47
00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.849
Open a group to examine its current
research status and identify

48
00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:21.730
areas that may need guidance.

49
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:25.386
The Milestones section helps advisers
follow the progress of a

50
00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:26.211
research group.

51
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.750
Here, you can review completed
activities, ongoing requirements, and

52
00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.271
upcoming research tasks.

53
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.544
Some milestones may require an adviser
review or approval before the

54
00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.612
group can proceed.

55
00:02:38.204 --> 00:02:41.513
By checking these records, you can
identify which requirements have

56
00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:43.870
been completed and which still need
attention.

57
00:02:44.462 --> 00:02:47.446
Your review applies to the exact
authorized requirement.

58
00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:51.103
It does not replace another required
faculty review or the

59
00:02:51.149 --> 00:02:52.891
coordinator's separate decision.

60
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.948
The Documents section provides access
to research files associated

61
00:02:56.983 --> 00:02:57.772
with this group.

62
00:02:58.365 --> 00:03:01.627
Expand the manuscript version history
and distinguish the current

63
00:03:01.673 --> 00:03:03.241
version from earlier copies.

64
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:07.955
Check version numbers, dates, status,
and the available Preview and

65
00:03:08.001 --> 00:03:09.116
Download controls.

66
00:03:09.545 --> 00:03:12.993
We will inspect the submitted PDF in
the review workspace next.

67
00:03:13.423 --> 00:03:16.685
This keeps the submitted content and
its recorded feedback in the

68
00:03:16.743 --> 00:03:18.299
same review context.

69
00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.919
The Reviews section brings together
manuscripts assigned to you for

70
00:03:21.988 --> 00:03:22.975
academic review.

71
00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:26.748
Select an active assignment to open
the submitted manuscript and its

72
00:03:26.795 --> 00:03:27.805
review workspace.

73
00:03:28.397 --> 00:03:31.427
Before providing a decision, confirm
that you're examining the

74
00:03:31.462 --> 00:03:35.003
correct document version and review
the research content carefully.

75
00:03:35.432 --> 00:03:39.031
An older approved copy or an earlier
revision request does not

76
00:03:39.089 --> 00:03:41.423
describe a newly submitted manuscript.

77
00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:45.841
Select a passage in this text-based
PDF and attach a constructive

78
00:03:45.876 --> 00:03:46.410
comment.

79
00:03:47.002 --> 00:03:50.148
Post the comment, then review the
recommendation choices:

80
00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:54.839
approve the version, request minor
revision, request major revision,

81
00:03:55.048 --> 00:03:56.348
or reject the version.

82
00:03:56.778 --> 00:03:59.343
For this example, choose minor
revision.

83
00:03:59.843 --> 00:04:03.581
Enter overall feedback explaining the
required changes and submit

84
00:04:03.627 --> 00:04:04.730
the permanent decision.

85
00:04:05.415 --> 00:04:08.922
Posting a comment and submitting the
review are separate actions.

86
00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.888
After the researcher submits a revised
manuscript, return to the

87
00:04:12.935 --> 00:04:14.305
same group's review record.

88
00:04:14.804 --> 00:04:17.625
This prepared later version belongs to
the same study;

89
00:04:18.055 --> 00:04:20.934
it is not an adviser editing the
researcher's submission.

90
00:04:21.526 --> 00:04:25.032
Compare the version information and
previous feedback, then open the

91
00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:25.914
current assignment.

92
00:04:26.414 --> 00:04:29.374
Add a short comment and approve the
version when the work meets the

93
00:04:29.432 --> 00:04:30.106
requirement.

94
00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:34.006
Other required faculty reviews and
workflow conditions may still

95
00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:34.842
remain.

96
00:04:35.433 --> 00:04:38.568
Some research documents may also
require the adviser's formal

97
00:04:38.614 --> 00:04:39.241
endorsement.

98
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:43.455
After completing the necessary review,
open the eligible document

99
00:04:43.514 --> 00:04:45.139
and follow the signing process.

100
00:04:45.638 --> 00:04:48.959
Review the document, position your
signature, and complete the

101
00:04:49.017 --> 00:04:50.294
required confirmation.

102
00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:54.230
ADVISIO preserves the signed document
as a separate record,

103
00:04:54.439 --> 00:04:57.016
maintaining the original document and
its history.

104
00:04:57.608 --> 00:05:01.509
Confirm your password and authorize
signing of this exact PDF.

105
00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:05.097
The saved signed copy has its own
verification record.

106
00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:08.533
This signature does not replace other
required institutional

107
00:05:08.568 --> 00:05:09.427
approvals.

108
00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:13.342
The Consultations section helps
advisers organize discussions with

109
00:05:13.365 --> 00:05:14.410
their research groups.

110
00:05:15.002 --> 00:05:18.961
Here, you can review consultation
requests, scheduled meetings, and

111
00:05:19.008 --> 00:05:20.354
their available details.

112
00:05:20.946 --> 00:05:24.650
When a consultation requires a
response, use the appropriate action

113
00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:26.078
to manage the request.

114
00:05:26.763 --> 00:05:30.293
Confirmed schedules help both the
adviser and researchers keep track

115
00:05:30.351 --> 00:05:31.640
of upcoming discussions.

116
00:05:32.232 --> 00:05:34.844
Approving the schedule records a
planned consultation;

117
00:05:35.215 --> 00:05:38.246
it does not certify that the meeting
has already taken place.

118
00:05:38.931 --> 00:05:41.892
Calendar provides another view of
upcoming activities.

119
00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.937
For an online consultation, use the
available meeting link when it

120
00:05:45.983 --> 00:05:47.016
is time to join.

121
00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:50.650
This recording does not open a live
meeting or record participant

122
00:05:50.685 --> 00:05:51.602
conversations.

123
00:05:52.032 --> 00:05:54.667
Switch to a separate completed
demonstration session.

124
00:05:55.166 --> 00:05:59.323
Open its notes, record the meeting
summary and adviser feedback, and

125
00:05:59.404 --> 00:06:00.925
list the agreed action items.

126
00:06:01.354 --> 00:06:04.663
Save the consultation history so the
group has a reference for its

127
00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:05.720
next tasks.

128
00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.236
Previous consultations and recorded
group activities provide context

129
00:06:10.271 --> 00:06:12.035
when monitoring research progress.

130
00:06:12.627 --> 00:06:16.343
By reviewing earlier feedback,
milestones, and submission events,

131
00:06:16.656 --> 00:06:19.663
advisers can follow the group's
development and determine which

132
00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.556
concerns have already been addressed.

133
00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:24.052
Consultation notes provide guidance;

134
00:06:24.365 --> 00:06:28.034
they remain distinct from a formal
manuscript or workflow decision.

135
00:06:28.633 --> 00:06:32.290
Open the group's Defense section to
inspect readiness indicators and

136
00:06:32.383 --> 00:06:34.206
any accessible session details.

137
00:06:34.891 --> 00:06:37.909
The displayed conditions distinguish
completed requirements from

138
00:06:37.979 --> 00:06:40.069
pending approvals and missing
documents.

139
00:06:40.754 --> 00:06:42.855
Adviser guidance supports preparation;

140
00:06:43.227 --> 00:06:45.526
it does not release the official
defense result.

141
00:06:46.118 --> 00:06:49.624
Official Copies provides a separate
register of authorized academic

142
00:06:49.671 --> 00:06:50.239
copies.

143
00:06:50.832 --> 00:06:54.222
A saved visual signature does not
automatically publish an official

144
00:06:54.291 --> 00:06:56.126
copy into that register.

145
00:06:56.733 --> 00:07:00.239
ADVISIO also provides communication
tools for coordinating with

146
00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:00.971
researchers.

147
00:07:01.656 --> 00:07:05.011
Messages supports conversations with
research groups, allowing you

148
00:07:05.069 --> 00:07:07.879
to share reminders and follow up on
academic work.

149
00:07:08.564 --> 00:07:12.233
Inbox is available for formal
correspondence, including messages and

150
00:07:12.291 --> 00:07:14.636
documents that require a more
structured record.

151
00:07:15.321 --> 00:07:18.630
Check the saved message in the
conversation and inspect the formal

152
00:07:18.676 --> 00:07:20.928
thread's participants and reply
controls.

153
00:07:21.613 --> 00:07:25.038
These demonstration messages remain
inside the isolated local

154
00:07:25.085 --> 00:07:25.990
workspace.

155
00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:29.748
Calendar helps you review upcoming
academic activities.

156
00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.533
Profile and Settings provide the
available account and workspace

157
00:07:33.579 --> 00:07:34.369
preferences.

158
00:07:34.868 --> 00:07:37.724
Return to Overview to check your
assigned groups and pending

159
00:07:37.771 --> 00:07:38.746
responsibilities.

160
00:07:39.431 --> 00:07:43.053
Regular follow-up connects advising
requests, research progress,

161
00:07:43.227 --> 00:07:46.850
manuscript decisions, and consultation
records without replacing the

162
00:07:46.896 --> 00:07:50.437
separate permissions and academic
responsibilities of other roles.

163
00:07:51.033 --> 00:07:54.133
That concludes the ADVISIO Faculty
Adviser walkthrough.

164
00:07:54.818 --> 00:07:57.430
From accepting groups to reviewing
revisions and recording

165
00:07:57.477 --> 00:08:01.285
consultation feedback, the workspace
helps you guide researchers and

166
00:08:01.343 --> 00:08:03.990
preserve a clear history of their
academic work.
